# Language direction and open questions

[[hql]] favors typed functional expressions and composition. These sketches
illustrate intent only; neither is accepted by the bootstrap parser:

```hql
alice : Doc = [[alice]]
```

```hql
knowledge
| graph
```

`[[..]]` is a doc reference, and `[[..]] -> [[..]] {..}` the link operator over
two of them; card-ness is a separate checked narrowing — see [[link-op]].
Functions, `.hql` module
imports, value construction, transformations, constraint validation, and typed
results belong to the intended scope. [[hmd-integration]] describes how partial
header schemas could contribute structural/type information.

## Recorded direction

The [example corpus](../../examples/README.md) records current design inputs.
Bare typed/inferred bindings are preferred; let is an alternative. A program
returns its last expression; rendering and explicit output are separate.
Cells close over explicit card environments, with isolated local bindings.
See [program values](../models/behavior/program-values.md).

Significant relationships are Relation Cards. `cards | typed Relation | graph`
is a core example. Knowledge includes evidence, provenance and conflicting
claims; Graph is one projection and HmdGraph is a presentation value. See the
[knowledge model](../models/domain/knowledge.md).

## Deliberately unresolved

- Function syntax, application, binding, pipeline desugaring, and precedence.
- Type inference, structural versus nominal records, schema checking, optional
  and unknown header fields, polymorphism, and numeric representation.
- Card identity, namespace context, unresolved/ambiguous references, graph value
  semantics, and the concrete host adapter interface.
- Module loading, effects and resource limits, transformation application,
  constraints/proofs, HMD-producing expressions, diagram-producing expressions,
  and richer computational cells.
- Specialized HMD fences such as `hql#query`, `hql#eval`, and `hql#declare`,
  including effect policy, dependency order, and exact presentation types.
  Lexical capture and value/context separation are recorded above.

Bootstrap `i64`, `f64`, `+`, and the 256-literal bound prove
[[first-milestone]]; they do not settle these questions. Float is now a working
bootstrap type, but decimal semantics, rounding and a numeric tower are not. There is no theorem prover, graph implementation,
HMD renderer, module system, or large standard library in this repository.

## Type vocabulary to leave room for

Future foundations include Date/DateTime, Option[T], Result[T,E],
List[T], Map[K,V], Section, Block, Ref[T] and Namespace, with records, ADTs,
pattern matching and refinement. Prefer explicit optional/error values over
pervasive null. String/Str naming, generic brackets and concrete schema syntax
remain open. Formal direction uses constraint and
satisfaction vocabulary; solver-backed or dependent checking is not bootstrap
work. Reading is pure; transformations construct values and persistence is an
explicit future effect.
